#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147310 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d058486e-3e14-5649-815a-7730311c5aec" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Recurrence Relation For an Exponential Growth or Decay Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "f47ee36e-c497-5f63-9e2b-b873af5600e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-6671" :question/problem "Let $y =\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n}$ be a series solution to the equation $y'-3y=0$.\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients $a_n$, where $n=0,1,2 \\ldots$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $y'(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′}(x) &= (∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n})^{′} \\\\\n&= (a_{0} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n})^{′} \\\\\n&= 0 + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and $y'(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(n = 1)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1} - 3∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m = n-1$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(m = 0)^(∞)(m + 1)a_{m + 1}x^{m} - 3∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(n = 0)^(∞)(n + 1)a_{n + 1}x^{n} - 3∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0$, we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(n = 0)^(∞)(n + 1)a_{n + 1}x^{n} - ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)3a_{n}x^{n} &= 0 \\\\\n∑_(n = 0)^(∞)[(n + 1)a_{n + 1}x^{n} - 3a_{n}x^{n}] &= 0 \\\\\n∑_(n = 0)^(∞)[(n + 1)a_{n + 1} - 3a_{n}]x^{n} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n(n+1) a_{n+1} -3 a_n = 0\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} =\\dfrac{3 a_n}{n+1}, \\qquad n= 0,1,2 \\ldots\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147311 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1980ddeb-37bf-5234-8888-f8292e2c9405" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Recurrence Relation For a Second-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "5466a51e-7dc5-55e6-a269-869cc7b94e83" :question/math-academy-id "e-6672" :question/problem "Let $y =\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n}$ be a series solution to the equation $2y''+y=0$. Find $f(n)$, given that the recurrence relation for $a_n$ can be written as\n\n$a_{n+2} = \\dfrac{a_n}{f(n)}, \\qquad n= 0,1,2\\ldots$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $y'(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′}(x) &= (∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n})^{′} \\\\\n&= (a_{0} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n})^{′} \\\\\n&= 0 + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find $y''(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{″}(x) &= (∑_(n = 1)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1})^{′} \\\\\n&= (a_{1} + ∑_(n = 2)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1})^{′} \\\\\n&= 0 + ∑_(n = 2)^(∞)n(n - 1)a_{n}x^{n - 2} \\\\\n&= ∑_(n = 2)^(∞)n(n - 1)a_{n}x^{n - 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and $y''(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n2\\sum_{n=2}^\\infty n (n-1) a_{n} x^{n-2} +\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^{n} = 0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m = n-2$. This gives\n\n$$\n2\\sum_{m=0}^\\infty (m+2) (m+1) a_{m+2} x^{m} +\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^{n} = 0\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n2\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty (n+2) (n+1) a_{n+2} x^{n} +\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^{n} = 0\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0$, we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(n = 0)^(∞)2(n + 2)(n + 1)a_{n + 2}x^{n} + ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n} &= 0 \\\\\n∑_(n = 0)^(∞)[2(n + 2)(n + 1)a_{n + 2}x^{n} + a_{n}x^{n}] &= 0 \\\\\n∑_(n = 0)^(∞)[2(n + 2)(n + 1)a_{n + 2} + a_{n}]x^{n} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n2(n+2)(n+1) a_{n+2} +a_n = 0\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+2} = -\\dfrac{a_n}{2(n+1)(n+2)}, \\qquad n= 0,1,2 \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(n)=-2(n+1)(n+2)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147312 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ab3f10-aca4-5094-98d2-0de9c11fd711" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Recurrence Relation For a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "d8617bae-7f0f-50d3-8b1a-23b7622956b0" :question/math-academy-id "e-6673" :question/problem "Let $y =\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n}$ be a series solution to the equation $y' +4xy = 0$.\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients $a_n$, where $n=1,2,3 \\ldots$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $y'(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′}(x) &= (∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n})^{′} \\\\\n&= (a_{0} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n})^{′} \\\\\n&= ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and $y'(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(n = 1)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1} + 4x∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n} &= 0 \\\\\n∑_(n = 1)^(∞)na_{n}x^{n - 1} + ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)4a_{n}x^{n + 1} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m = n-1$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\sum_{m=0}^\\infty (m+1) a_{m+1} x^{m} + \\sum_{n=0}^\\infty 4a_n x^{n+1} =0\n$$\n\nNow, in the second series, we change the index of the summation by writing\n\n$$\nm = n+1\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\sum_{m=0}^\\infty (m+1) a_{m+1} x^{m} + \\sum_{m=1}^\\infty 4a_{m-1} x^{m} =0\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty (n+1) a_{n+1} x^{n} + \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty 4 a_{n-1} x^{n} =0\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n$. So, we take out the term $n = 0$ from the left-hand side:\n\n$$\na_1 + \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty (n+1) a_{n+1} x^{n} + \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty 4a_{n-1} x^{n} = 0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{1} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)[(n + 1)a_{n + 1}x^{n} + 4a_{n - 1}x^{n}] &= 0 \\\\\na_{1} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)[(n + 1)a_{n + 1} + 4a_{n - 1}]x^{n} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of $x^n$, we obtain\n\n$$\na_1 = 0, \\qquad (n+1) a_{n+1} = -4a_{n-1}\n$$\n\nSolving for $a_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = -\\dfrac{4a_{n-1}}{n+1}, \\quad n=1,2,3 \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recurrence relation is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = -\\dfrac{4a_{n-1}}{n+1}, \\quad a_1=0, \\quad n=1,2,3 \\ldots\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index equals to $0$, since $a_1=0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ab3f10-aca4-5094-98d2-0de9c11fd711" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Recurrence Relation For a First-Order Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97c58615-eabe-56a5-8d57-5232a34e01a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n + 1} = 4(n + 1)a_{n - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146702} {:answer/id #uuid "b86755ee-c3fd-5fb0-a0df-07ffdc9d6979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n + 1} =-\\frac{a_{n - 1}}{4n + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146703} {:answer/id #uuid "06510bc2-4240-594e-89af-34233914a4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n + 1} = \\frac{4a_{n - 1}}{n + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146704} {:answer/id #uuid "20e015e5-d612-53cb-a6f7-bb7752c9afa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n + 1} = - (a_{n - 1})/(4(n + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146705} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3d3cce-09b1-5dc1-9cf4-5962f7619d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n + 1} =-4na_{n - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20e015e5-d612-53cb-a6f7-bb7752c9afa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a_{n + 1} = - (a_{n - 1})/(4(n + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146705} :answer-field/id #uuid "026d0872-6d45-5b59-bf44-af1b00d0735a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146701}] :question/id #uuid "13a532bd-febd-559f-9c5a-ce92173249b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-64541" :question/problem "Let $y = ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $4y^{′} + xy = 0$.\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients $a_{n}$, where $n = 1, 2, 3, …$"}]}
